**Evaluating stack behavior**

After a successful update, I notice the optimistic deletion and approval can lead to the fallback disappearing. This allows the currentStackRequest to move on to the next pending item, which is good. But when there's a failure, the optimistic deletion means the status reverts to pending, thus including it back in activePending. I need to ensure that the stackIndex isn’t auto-reset when the length of activePending shrinks—though it probably will be okay in practice.
